tracked and small -- git already is their backup, so they are deliberately NOT copied here.

WHY THE ROOT IS OUTSIDE THE TREE. Default `${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/mr-backup`: a
machine singleton that survives `git clean -xfd` and `git worktree remove`. An earlier draft put the
copies under $MEM, which deletes the insurance along with the accident -- the whole point of EARS-1.

WHY MR_BACKUP_ROOT IS AN ALLOWED OVERRIDE while mr-selfcheck deliberately REFUSES an equivalent
MR_SELFCHECK_MEM: mr-selfcheck is a GATE, where an override is a surface for greening production
vacuously. mr-backup is a DATA COPIER, not a verdict -- an override cannot fabricate a pass, only
redirect where bytes land, and a misdirected root is caught by mr-selfcheck's drift check, which
reads the DEFAULT root and ignores MR_BACKUP_ROOT entirely. Without it every selftest and teeth run
would write into the real root: the "selftest pollutes the real corpus" anti-pattern this corpus
already carries two guards against.

ROOT SAFETY -- BOTH checks run before anything is written OR pruned, and neither creates a directory:
  1. the resolved root's basename must be LITERALLY `mr-backup` (`.../mr-backup`,
     `<tmpdir>/mr-backup` pass; `$HOME`, `/tmp`, `notbackup`, `$HOME/backup-scratch` do not). The
     prune unlinks 8-digit-named DIRECTORIES, so without this `MR_BACKUP_ROOT=$HOME` -- a plausible
     typo for `$HOME/.local/state/mr-backup` -- would let it delete real 8-digit-named directories
     under $HOME. Fixtures do not get a concession here: they NEST their own root as
     `<tmpdir>/mr-backup`. A substring or `-`/`_`-token match is explicitly REJECTED, because it
     admits `$HOME/backup` and `$HOME/backup-old`, and the entire job of this check is to bound
     what the prune loop may unlink to directories it can prove are this tool's own.
  2. the root must not sit inside a git working tree (walk up looking for a `.git`) -- restating
     the paragraph above as an illegal state rather than a convention.

THE CANONICAL-SOURCE BOUNDARY (parse-don't-validate, enforced HERE, never at the call site). With
MR_BACKUP_ROOT UNSET (production) a snapshot source must be EXACTLY one of the two canonical
absolute paths by os.path.realpath; anything else is exit 0 plus one `skip:` line on stderr. With
